07:00","id":1543367,"title":"","content":"I did not know that, but I'm not a big follower of the clan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-08T16:30:18-07:00","id":1543368,"title":"","content":"The majority of the Assamite Sorcerer caste is supposed to be descended from Ur-Shulgi. I suppose that doesn't guarantee that he himself embraced a large number of childer rather than it being the work of his descendants, but it seems likely to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-08T16:34:44-07:00","id":1543369,"title":"","content":"Yes Ur-Shugi is supposed to be the second Childe of Haqim and two thirds of the sorcerer's caste trace themselves to him. But we only know Al-Ashrad as a direct childe of the monster from the lore. But I would think that he has two or three more direct childer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-08T16:36:30-07:00","id":1543370,"title":"","content":"Mithras has sired at least 5 or 6 childer himself if we don't count the two from the Victorian era as there's some confusion. It seems that most of the English Ventrue come from his lineage and that seems reasonable as London and to a lesser extent England is his domain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-08T18:00:55-07:00","id":1543376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543299-which-kindred-is-a-prolific-sire#post1543299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a fun thread of which Kindred do you think has the most childer. We know Michael has at least 4 childer from Rome and Constantinople and Mithras has at least 5 or six that we know. So what do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>Lodin has, I believe, a dozen in the Chicago by Night 1st edition. Who knows if he created any outside of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6423-higgipedia","name":"higgipedia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6423_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-08T19:28:54-07:00","id":1543380,"title":"","content":"He sired at least four to six kindred in the Chicago area and he might have have another elsewhere. He was or is quite prolific.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-09T13:32:22-07:00","id":1543438,"title":"","content":"Le sigh... I was a fool to try to edit it<br /> Here we go again!<br /> So...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543299-which-kindred-is-a-prolific-sire#post1543299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a fun thread of which Kindred do you think has the most childer. We know Michael has at least 4 childer from Rome and Constantinople and Mithras has at least 5 or six that we know. So what do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>I thin kthe winer is the Tzimisce <b>Noriz</b>, <b>the Corrupter of Legions, </b>5th Generation Child of Djavakhi<br /> His official bio in Transylvania By Night (later expanded in Dark Ages Clan Novel 13: Tzimisce and : Clanbook: Tzimisce Revised) mentions his goal was ascendance to the most powerful creature of the Carpathians. To this end, <u><i><b>he sired legions of childer</b></i></u>, who were instructed to consume the souls of as many vampires as possible, and was known to begin wars against rivals by the slightest provocation and encouraged infighting among his brood in order to weed out the weak. Noriz's weakest childer became his tools; his strongest childer became his enemies, who improved his own martial skills<br /> His Child, Lugoj, The Blood-Breaker got so fed up with this basically his behavior (that many Tzimisce Elder followed just not in this large scale) sparked the Tzimsice Anarch Revolt\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543299-which-kindred-is-a-prolific-sire?p=1543365#post1543365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC Baba Yaga is the only 4th gen that created an entire clan (every Nos descends from her).</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not entirely true, many sources among Libellus Sanguinis 4: Thieves in the Night, claims Medusa, the Gorgon, the Matriarch is the soruce of the Clan and she was the broodmate of Baba Yaga and Melachoate and the three escaped the Blood Bond, tho' only one is named, <b>Angiwar </b>(from Dark Ages Europe and Encyclopaedia Vampirica) and Nuckalavee the Skinless may be the ancestor to the Parisii breed of the Nosferatu whose have translucent skin\u200b<br /> But Baba Yaga's descendants sure sired many, especially <b>Gutka, the Salt Queen</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-09T17:55:50-07:00","id":1543470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543299-which-kindred-is-a-prolific-sire?p=1543380#post1543380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He sired at least four to six kindred in the Chicago area and he might have have another elsewhere. He was or is quite prolific.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eleven, not counting any that might show up in other books.<br /> <br /> From <i>Chicago by Night</i> (1991), he sired:<br /> Tommy Hinds, Edgar Drummond, Brennon Thornhill - Killed in the events of <i>Under a Blood Red Moon</i> (1993)<br /> Joseph Peterson, Exiled sometime after 2009 per <i>Chicago by Night</i> (2020)<br /> Jacob Schumpeter, Recently missing in 2019/20 per <i>Chicago by Night</i> (2020)\u200b<br /> \u200bLorraine Matthews, Recently missing as of 2020 per <i>Chicago by Night</i> (2020)\u200b<br /> Alphonse Capone, thought missing, fate revealed in <i>The Chicago Folios</i> (2020)<br /> Horatio Ballard, Edward Neally, Kevin Jackson, Bobby Weatherbottom, still around per <i>Chicago by Night</i> (2020)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6423-higgipedia","name":"higgipedia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6423_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-09T18:49:44-07:00","id":1543479,"title":"","content":"Lodin is certainly prolific considering he is not an elder by any means.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-12T14:14:45-07:00","id":1543633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543299-which-kindred-is-a-prolific-sire?p=1543479#post1543479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lodin is certainly prolific considering he is not an elder by any means.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most definitely prolific, probably the most prolific I know of, especially considering his age.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-12T14:53:35-07:00","id":1543642,"title":"","content":"I'm just surprised that he had time to sire so many childer and be a effective Prince of Chicago. Though I guess his elder childer would be doing some of the mentoring of Ventrue neonates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-12T23:25:30-07:00","id":1543667,"title":"","content":"Oh! It just occurred to me, the former Prince Michaela of New York was said to be siring so many childer for the holding action against the Sabbat that Manhattan was awash in her fledglings. They were short-lived cannon fodder rather than carefully chosen progeny, but she's probably the most prolific character I can recall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-13T12:14:08-07:00","id":1543698,"title":"","content":"No wonder Calebros was tapped as a placeholder Prince when Michaela vanished. He would be a smarter leader.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-14T09:24:56-07:00","id":1543758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543299-which-kindred-is-a-prolific-sire?p=1543698#post1543698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No wonder Calebros was tapped as a placeholder Prince when Michaela vanished. He would be a smarter leader.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, specially since Aislling Sturbridge wouldn't really bother wanting to be prince, Calebros is certainly a better leader than Michaela.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T12:01:35-07:00","id":1543898,"title":"","content":"I could see Aisling Sturbridge as an effective Prince, but it would cut into her time for learning more estoric matters and she loves that stuff,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"20